{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings","id":584456,"title":"Narrowness of 2e Seemings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-09T03:31:25-07:00","id":584456,"title":"Narrowness of 2e Seemings","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This is probably a pretty terrible way to start on the forums, but this is... honestly making me really nervous. (Granted, a lot of things do.) </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Basically, the five seemings in 2e, while all great and viable ways to escape from Arcadia are... very, very narrow. 1e gives the examples of Changelings who escaped by tricking their Keepers, challenging them to a game for their freedom, or even waiting out their limited-duration durance. In 2e, we only have these five Seemings, which it seems like a lot of characters won\u2019t fit into. I\u2019m just really on-edge because\u2026 I feel like I could be missing something? Or like I MUST be missing something. (Which is really pretty plausible, because, again, first post here. Haven\u2019t seen much. Hi!)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Are the Seemings a non-exhaustive list? Is there another Seeming for the duelist who challenged his Keeper to a fencing match and won his freedom, for the Storyteller and player of this character to design? Should the character be shoehorned into an ill-fitting Seeming that doesn\u2019t really resonate with how he escaped but is the closest match? (Ogre COULD fit there, but what of the girl who bested her keeper in a chess match?) Or are the five Seemings written prescriptive - is the ONLY way to escape to spurn humanity/become a leader/betray someone/become one with the land/remake yourself with your work? Are Keepers just unaffected, or unwilling to let people escape by other means? (Loopholes in the ancient Contracts which let them keep slaves, maybe?)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At the moment I\u2019m just\u2026 nervous, because it seems like this is a heavy constraint on what kinds of characters are possible. Maybe I\u2019m missing how flexible the new Seemings can be, and I\u2019d love to be proven wrong - but until then I\u2019m very much on-edge whenever I think of 2e. (And it\u2019s PROBABLY unjustified.) </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I guess I\u2019m just hoping you guys can put my mind at ease. Sorry for being so demanding.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T04:05:45-07:00","id":584498,"title":"","content":"Don't worry about it, you're not being demanding. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I feel like your problem is that you're being too vague with your character ideas while being too specific with your interpretation of how Seemings work. The new Seeming set up isn't about &quot;You performed Action X, you are now a Fairest (or whatever).&quot; I'd say a better way of looking at the issue is to figure <i>how</i> your character views their escape and what about themselves they feel they're letting go of.<br /> <br /> So let's take your duelist (or chess player) example. What's the focus of that conflict in the character's eyes? What did they lose in the fight (or chess match)? When I say lose, I don't mean like &quot;got an arm lopped off&quot; or &quot;lost X in a bet,&quot; but the psychological cost of victory. So the sword fight (or the chess match) might be about embracing your Id/instincts, letting go of your Self, repurposing the &quot;gifts&quot; of your durance, etc.<br /> <br /> Don't focus on what you did, but rather how you did it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T04:29:26-07:00","id":584506,"title":"","content":"... that does make a lot of sense, though it also - as pretty obvious by the fact I <i>missed</i> it - it's a bit hard to even think what that could... be? Like- hrm. I suppose it doesn't make for a very interesting story if nothing WAS lost. But... I guess I'm struggling to think of what the answer to 'how' could be, in a lot of those scenarios? What do you give up by going Ferris Bueller and making them think you hadn't left? Or by seducing one of their loyal servants into slipping you the keys?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T04:34:45-07:00","id":584512,"title":"","content":"You can have a character with no seeming if you have a method of escape that doesn't seem to fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T04:41:12-07:00","id":584514,"title":"","content":"Also, there's going to be at least one, maybe 2 more Seemings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T04:48:37-07:00","id":584517,"title":"","content":"THIS IS ALL NEW INFORMATION which I am happy to hear. Whee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T06:19:45-07:00","id":584605,"title":"","content":"As far as I'm aware, there's still six Seemings, plus a potential Loyalist one. Not sure why we keep talking about five...<br /> <br /> Anyways! I don't see why tricking your Keeper, or challenging him to a duel, aren't still viable. Lets take the Fairest for a moment, with their &quot;leadership&quot; theme going on. They rally others to support their escape. If they tricked the Keeper, they were able to trick them by getting the fellow changelings to side against them. In a duel challenge, perhaps it was a situation where the support literally fed the Fairest's and made them stronger.<br /> <br /> Now, lets look at this from a Darkling angle. Instead of being a leader, they use lies and misdirection to win the game of trickery, and all backstabby, perhaps with a touch of iron or poision, or the duel.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, its mostly just your approach. Are you a leader of people? Are you backstabby? Prefer brute force or relying on your instincts? You can trick people or win a duel with any of the above. Its easy enough to fit almost any escape into any Seeming, imho, with a little twist or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-09-2015, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T06:27:38-07:00","id":584618,"title":"","content":"There's the former 6 (Beast, Darkling, Elemental, Fairest, Ogre and Wizened), a seventh in the Dark Eras book and posibly an Eigth to be posted someday in the blog. Apart from that there's been talk about turning the Loyalist from always Seemingless to a Seeming of their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 07-09-2015, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T06:44:31-07:00","id":584648,"title":"","content":"(Beast, Fairest, Elemental, Darkling, Wizened, Ogre. Yup. Six. Oops.)<br /> <br /> So basically the issue with your point is- well, the first is that Darklings aren't just 'tricksy darkness poisoners' anymore - they are DEFINED as &quot;those who betrayed an ally to escape from Arcadia&quot;. If they challenged them alone, then there is no-one to martyr yourself for, nor to betray.<br /> <br /> The problem is that as a result of these six seemings defining how you escape, the narratives OF these seemings have to be forced into it, or else... I guess you don't have a Seeming?<br /> <br /> Consider the duel in which it is simply the Changeling against the Keeper - a proper duel, for the Changeling's freedom. They are not flowing away as an Elemental, backstabbing as a Darkling, martyring themselves as a Fairest, betraying an ally as Darkling, denouncing humanity as a Beast, or remaking themselves as a Wizened.<br /> <br /> Do you bs your explanation as a Wizened (the... reliance on swordplay is at least a CRAFT, but they're not really remaking themselves...), not get a Seeming at all, or is the fact the character doesn't fit into the 6 seemings mean he's unplayable?<br /> <br /> (I mean from earlier answers here it seems like 'not getting a seeming' is the answer. Which is... a bit weird.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: ... Also I just realised - does this mean Loyalists would have unique Seeming, as they didn't escape?<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: Also I forgot Potential Answer 4 - that this situation calls for the Storyteller's creation of another more fitting seeming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","user":"Taveena","date":". 07-09-2015, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T08:02:12-07:00","id":584739,"title":"","content":"Alright, so let's take the escape via duel example. I could see that working for pretty much all of them depending on how you run with it.<br /> <br /> Beast: Focus on embracing your instincts to win.<br /> Elemental: Reverse of Beast, &quot;no mind,&quot; Zen, etc.<br /> <br /> Darkling: Victory by sacrificing others, doesn't mean you had to have killed or left others behind on your way out (though you easily could have), possibly just burned bridges somehow<br /> Fairest: Heroic victory, probably wound up freeing more than just yourself<br /> <br /> Ogre: Burning spirit, berserk fury, overwhelming passion and emotion.<br /> Wizened: THE RIDDLE OF STEEL ...tbh I'm still wrapping my head around the escape concepts of Wizened and how their abandonment of the Self parallels the Elementals. For now I'd probably go with something focusing on your failing flesh/body and salvation through raw skill. Let the weird replacement of skin and bone with steel become more of a side effect of Arcadia (which is basically what all the Seemings are when you get down to it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T08:04:13-07:00","id":584741,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that David H, the developer on the project, has said he is going to include a sudebar in the Seeming section that makes it absolutely clear that the Seeming backgrounds and escapes are archetypal examples, not the only way a character can become that Seeming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T09:03:05-07:00","id":584811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=584739#post584739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">tbh I'm still wrapping my head around the escape concepts of Wizened and how their abandonment of the Self parallels the Elementals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually love that parallel! Where an Elemental abandons her identity, a Wizened abandons his body. Where an Elemental becomes one with the environment, a Wizened becomes one with a craft or trade. Where a Wizened becomes the perfect artist, an Elemental becomes art. So cool!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T09:07:10-07:00","id":584816,"title":"","content":"They run on story logic. If you can think of even a flimsy reason that a given escape attempt resulted in a seeming, you're good. <br /> <br /> I bet if I tried I could find a way to give a given changeling any seeming I liked using the same backstory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T09:15:00-07:00","id":584823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=584811#post584811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually love that parallel! Where an Elemental abandons her identity, a Wizened abandons his body. Where an Elemental becomes one with the environment, a Wizened becomes one with a craft or trade. Where a Wizened becomes the perfect artist, an Elemental becomes art. So cool!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this plus AA's post in the Wizened thread I think cover the divide pretty well. Elementals let go of their Self, Wizened tether their Self to their craft.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=584816#post584816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I bet if I tried I could find a way to give a given changeling any seeming I liked using the same backstory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh you absolutely could, that's the trick. Your Seeming is entirely how you look at your escape.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T09:32:37-07:00","id":584828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=584823#post584823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, this plus AA's post in the Wizened thread I think cover the divide pretty well. Elementals let go of their Self, Wizened tether their Self to their craft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think Arts said it better than I could have, in a more concise way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=584823#post584823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh you absolutely could, that's the trick. Your Seeming is entirely how you look at your escape.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, although you should also consider how your character's background contributes to their outlook on their escape. I think that's why the examples come off as narrow to many - they do paint a very specific picture, but it's meant to inspire you to paint your own picture, not limit your palette.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T09:48:14-07:00","id":584841,"title":"","content":"Mine idea of Seemings based on duel Escape:<ul><li><b>Beast:</b> Blind rage, animalistic power overpowering the Keeper</li> <li><b>Elemental:</b> Becoming &quot;one with the wind&quot;, you, literally, devolved youself to get lost in the fight, BECOMING WIND, so the Keeper could not hit you</li> <li><b>Darkling:</b> You made plan to challange to battle, only made other one fight for you and so you could escape.</li> <li><b>Fairest:</b> You rose the army of fellow changelings and to save them, you challange the Keeper - and won.</li> <li><b>Ogre:</b> You lost your heart in the fight. Literally.</li> <li><b>Wizened:</b> By spending next 20 years and training, you finally challanged Keeper when you become worn out weapon master.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-09-2015, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T09:54:04-07:00","id":584847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=584739#post584739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, so let's take the escape via duel example. I could see that working for pretty much all of them depending on how you run with it.<br /> <br /> Beast: Focus on embracing your instincts to win.<br /> Elemental: Reverse of Beast, &quot;no mind,&quot; Zen, etc.<br /> <br /> Darkling: Victory by sacrificing others, doesn't mean you had to have killed or left others behind on your way out (though you easily could have), possibly just burned bridges somehow<br /> Fairest: Heroic victory, probably wound up freeing more than just yourself<br /> <br /> Ogre: Burning spirit, berserk fury, overwhelming passion and emotion.<br /> Wizened: THE RIDDLE OF STEEL ...</div> </div> </div> </div>The fun thing about these is that some of them work for others just fine. Riddle of Steel, as you imply, works fine for Elemental and also for Fairest. Sacrifice of others works fine for Beast as much as Darkling. Berserk Fury works fine for Elemental or Beast.<br /> <br /> Plus, some alternatives:<br /> <br /> For Beast, breaking the rules of etiquette: you find a cold iron blade somewhere, or you gut punch them and run away while they're reeling.<br /> For Elemental, the ground betrayed the Keeper; you danced away and he kept tripping until you got enough openings and opportunities to wrest a win.<br /> For Darkling: you weren't supposed to be the duellist; you conned the other Changeling and took his place, and then won.<br /> For Fairest: the duel happened in the middle of an escape; your Keeper agreed to single combat for <i>all</i> of your companions, and you won.<br /> For Ogre: your Keeper kept scoring hits on you, but you just refused to feel them. He attacked more and more wildly, but you just wouldn't go down.<br /> For Wizened: your special skill isn't combat; it's trash talking. You kept talking and your Keeper couldn't focus on fighting anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=584739#post584739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">tbh I'm still wrapping my head around the escape concepts of Wizened and how their abandonment of the Self parallels the Elementals. For now I'd probably go with something focusing on your failing flesh/body and salvation through raw skill. Let the weird replacement of skin and bone with steel become more of a side effect of Arcadia (which is basically what all the Seemings are when you get down to it).</div> </div> </div> </div>It is very similar.<br /> <br /> The key difference between the Elemental and the Wizened, IMO, is that the Elemental transcends through unpredictability whereas the Wizened transcends through understanding. An Elemental says, &quot;You cannot expect everything, so expect nothing.&quot; A Wizened says, &quot;You cannot expect everything, but you can expect everything that matters.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T09:56:53-07:00","id":584851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=584847#post584847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The key difference between the Elemental and the Wizened, IMO, is that the Elemental transcends through unpredictability whereas the Wizened transcends through understanding. An Elemental says, &quot;You cannot expect everything, so expect nothing.&quot; A Wizened says, &quot;You cannot expect everything, but you can expect everything that matters.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, I like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T10:35:33-07:00","id":584866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taveena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=584506#post584506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or by seducing one of their loyal servants into slipping you the keys?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wizened is basically the easiest. Whatever you did to escape, chess playing, swordplay, running really fast, whatever? That's your Wizened's craft. Did your character decide &quot;I need to be really, really good at seducing people if I want to escape&quot;? Bam, Wizened. Would your character have formerly sneered at players and seducers, did they think it wasn't <i>appropriate</i><i>, civilized</i> behavior, but ended up sacrificing those concerns? You could make a Beast. Did you betray the servant? Did you fake genuine affection so they would lower their guard only to run away as soon as you had the keys in hands? Darkling. Did you inspire the servant? Did you make a stirring speech about how escaping was the only thing you could do, did you make puppy dog eyes, did you touch the servant's emotions such that they gave you the keys willingly? Fairest. Elemental would... let go of their ego, and subsume themselves into the concept of seduction, I guess? I'm having trouble seeing any other interpretation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taveena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=584648#post584648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically the issue with your point is- well, the first is that Darklings aren't just 'tricksy darkness poisoners' anymore - they are DEFINED as &quot;those who betrayed an ally to escape from Arcadia&quot;. If they challenged them alone, then there is no-one to martyr yourself for, nor to betray.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;In her mind, or in reality [...] It meant taking advantage of the situation and making the hard choice, not the right choice. And in that decision, she let shadows in, she accepted it in and abandoned the light and righteous path.&quot; If your character realized that they couldn't beat their keeper in a fair fight, if they decided to rely on trickery or poison, and if <i>that</i> was a significant choice on their part, that they now see themselves as less of an honest person... then they are totally a Darkling. The &quot;in her mind&quot; part is really important. You don't need to have literally pushed another changeling under your keeper's sword for a distraction. As long as the character did something they considered a betrayal, something dishonest, it works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taveena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=584506#post584506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider the duel in which it is simply the Changeling against the Keeper - a proper duel, for the Changeling's freedom. They are not flowing away as an Elemental, backstabbing as a Darkling, martyring themselves as a Fairest, betraying an ally as Darkling, denouncing humanity as a Beast, or remaking themselves as a Wizened.<br /> <br /> Do you bs your explanation as a Wizened (the... reliance on swordplay is at least a CRAFT, but they're not really remaking themselves...), not get a Seeming at all, or is the fact the character doesn't fit into the 6 seemings mean he's unplayable?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who's talking about Elementals flowing away? Sacrifice your ego, <i>become swordplay</i>.*<br /> <br /> All the Seemings represent a psychological transformation. The game assumes your character was <i>changed</i> in some way from this duel. They did something, they acted in a certain way and now they're different, or rather they <i>see themselves</i> as different and Arcadia, in its great generosity, acceded and changed the Changeling in a fitting way. If you just want your character to have fought a duel and not have any epiphany, no realization about what was holding them back, nothing transformative... then yes, you're in trouble.<br /> <br /> *Or take in the strength of a storm and use it to win. Whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","user":"Kazorh","date":". 07-09-2015, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T10:48:39-07:00","id":584875,"title":"","content":"Well if you want to trick your Keeper, I believe that Darklings and Fairest are perfect candidates for that. As a Darkling you could outwit them, while as a Fairest you could make them look like a fool in front of their peers. I can see how you might think the current write up sounds narrow, but I'll try to put a different spin on things here. There are different ways I imagine Seemings being able to escape their Keepers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Darkling - Cunning and deceit to outmaneuver your Keeper.<br /> <br /> Fairest - Public humiliation of your Keeper.<br /> <br /> Beast - Do something completely unexpected.<br /> <br /> Ogre - To hell with subtlety, just bum rush the exit<br /> <br /> Elemental - You stopped thinking only of yourself, that makes you infinitely more dangerous.<br /> <br /> Wizened - Your Keeper honed your skills to perfection, that was their mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-09-2015, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T10:57:39-07:00","id":584880,"title":"","content":"Can I just say how great it is to have one of these threads actually turn into a respectful and constructive discussion about how different concepts might fit into the various Seemings? This is really nice and quite refreshing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T12:07:31-07:00","id":584985,"title":"","content":"Personally I think it is a mistake to choose a seeming based soley on how they escaped. To me it should be based on how you endured your durance, what was your survival mechanism? The ogre responded to abuse by becoming mean, a hurt them before they hurt you philosophy. The elemental embraced 'they can't hurt you if you don't care'. The darkling took on a siege mentality, &quot;It's a dog eat dog world, trust no one because they will betray you&quot;. The wizened threw himself into his work, the ultimate work aholic. The fairest responded by putting themselves out, stepping up and focusing more on others as a way to protect themselves. I would say that the changes of the seeming were wrought by the wyrd in response to the traits embraced by the changeling. In a way a seeming is the first step to becoming one of the true fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T13:02:13-07:00","id":585055,"title":"","content":"Those who merely endure their durance are not enacting agency. One does not say &quot;Enough of this shit&quot; by saying &quot;Please sir, I want some more.&quot;<br /> <br /> [/petpeeve]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T15:34:23-07:00","id":585290,"title":"","content":"Choosing not to be broken by tragedy or abuse <i>is</i> an act of will. Tak's point is a good one. If you ever do stand up for yourself, you have to do so from some position of inner strength. One's strategy for reserving such is clearly important.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T16:07:57-07:00","id":585317,"title":"","content":"You don't choose that sort of crap. You don't decide what hurts and wounds or not. The idea that you can just take a traumatic event is a bold faced lie, a thing people <i>think</i> is done outside of the experience. You can only decide what happens after the fact. Some people are good at doing that, and even doing it quickly. Lots of people aren't.<br /> <br /> More on point, deciding to do something about your trauma <i>is</i> refusing to broken by your cirucmstances, or more accurately refusing to <i>continue</i> to be broken. It is, in fact, the only act of refusal that counts.<br /> <br /> You do not get away from the bad circumstance by <i>sitting in the middle of it and letting it happen</i>.<br /> <br /> And look, I admit to be stubborn on a lot of things, but I also admit bias usually. I'm biased here too, but I might as well make it clear: This is not something I grant to other people. This is something I do not believe in being flexible on. You don't handle trauma by just sitting through it. <i>You do <u><b>not</b></u> just handle trauma by enduring it. <b>You have to do something about it</b></i>.<br /> <br /> Sorry if no one likes me saying that, but it's something I'm not backing away from. I called it a pet peeve, but it's much deeper and sorer than that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T16:28:47-07:00","id":585338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=584985#post584985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I think it is a mistake to choose a seeming based soley on how they escaped. To me it should be based on how you endured your durance, what was your survival mechanism? The ogre responded to abuse by becoming mean, a hurt them before they hurt you philosophy. The elemental embraced 'they can't hurt you if you don't care'. The darkling took on a siege mentality, &quot;It's a dog eat dog world, trust no one because they will betray you&quot;. The wizened threw himself into his work, the ultimate work aholic. The fairest responded by putting themselves out, stepping up and focusing more on others as a way to protect themselves. I would say that the changes of the seeming were wrought by the wyrd in response to the traits embraced by the changeling. In a way a seeming is the first step to becoming one of the true fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it could be both. I mean the changelings we're hearing about are the ones who escaped and they did that by changing. There may be changelings who have developed seemings without escaping. What about a fairest who helped others escape by staying behind? Or a loyalist darkling who betrayed someone trying to escape? You can have extra points for switching those round somehow. And there may be some changelings who neither escaped nor committed themselves to hindering other changelings like those who just learnt to live there. But perhaps the moment someone gives up that part of himself and exchanges it for the thing the defines his seeming is the last time he can choose to escape?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T17:05:39-07:00","id":585385,"title":"","content":"All of the Seemings involve escaping the Fae, <i>at some point</i>. Nobody suggested that predation was acceptable nor that.inaction or acquiescence was admirable. Unless escape is immediate, however, surviving with enough of yourself left to matter and escape requires enduring torment. How you manage that defines your Seeming. How one managed to keep that piece of self until escape is obviously important to the character even <i>if</i> the final escape strategy <i>is </i>the only element to consider for choosing the Seeming. I think the idea of looking at that process holistically works well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T17:39:25-07:00","id":585441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585055#post585055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those who merely endure their durance are not enacting agency. One does not say &quot;Enough of this shit&quot; by saying &quot;Please sir, I want some more.&quot;<br /> <br /> [/petpeeve]</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially, that would make the character Seemingless. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T17:46:31-07:00","id":585478,"title":"","content":"Which is perfectly valid as a character concept! Can we as a group please remember that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-09-2015, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T18:18:18-07:00","id":585503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=584866#post584866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elemental would... let go of their ego, and subsume themselves into the concept of seduction, I guess? I'm having trouble seeing any other interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>A person with no ego has much more willingness to go with manipulation; their difficulty is in figuring out how to do it. The important moment for an Elemental whose escape pivots on seduction would be starting from, &quot;I am not the kind of person who would seduce someone,&quot; and just... letting go of that.<br /> <br /> You could also play up the chaotic aspect by having the seduction be an <i>accident</i> that you simply take credit for. You're escaping; the servant discovers you... and lets you go. You barely know who they were, but they were in love with you. If you've read Girl Genius (and this is a <b>spoiler</b>, and <b>kind of a climactic moment</b>, so I'll be vague), <a href=\"http://www.girlgeniusonline.com/comic.php?date=20061211\" target=\"_blank\">the moment when Lars, Agatha, and Klaus are all on the same page</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T18:41:30-07:00","id":585513,"title":"","content":"'Course, given this is Arcadia, an elemental could seduce the <i>lock</i>... <br /> <br /> There's also that Grimm tale with the girl chopping off her finger and grinding the bone down to make a key so she could sneak on out. Very different take on becoming the key, but still fits the theme. (I lean towards interpreting that as a Darkling maneuver, but you could argue that a few ways.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T19:51:32-07:00","id":585545,"title":"","content":"Once a thief always a thief. You were born white trash and you'll die white trash. While trauma can change a person it is persistent behavior that defines them, not the moment of being a victim. Arcadia would be filled with people who embraced their work as slaves, but the wyrd would only respond to those who persist and escape. I just think the method of escape would not define a person anymore than one act or even mistake does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T19:57:59-07:00","id":585546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585545#post585545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once a thief always a thief. You were born white trash and you'll die white trash. While trauma can change a person it is persistent behavior that defines them, not the moment of being a victim. Arcadia would be filled with people who embraced their work as slaves, but the wyrd would only respond to those who persist and escape. I just think the method of escape would not define a person anymore than one act or even mistake does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, no. Dr. House is an utter cynic and depressive, not a life coach; one can see a logical progression from &quot;thief&quot; to &quot;security specialist&quot;, but the specialist is still defined by stopping crimes, not committing them. Similarly, a businessman born in a trailer park is still living in an apartment, even if he likes and regularly visits his parents, thanking them for the virtues he used to succeed.<br /> <br /> Persistent behavior changes, particularly in response to extreme trauma. When one mentally associates a particular thought or action with freedom and self-determination, one is likely to continue that behavior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T20:05:39-07:00","id":585549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585545#post585545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arcadia would be filled with people who embraced their work as slaves, but the wyrd would only respond to those who persist and escape. I just think the method of escape would not define a person anymore than one act or even mistake does.</div> </div> </div> </div>The method of escape metaphysically redefined you as a new person made from the remains of what got you into Faerie and what the Others drew out of you. The method of escape is a formative experience that one carries into their new life as one of the Lost.<br /> <br /> You've partaken of Arcadia's capacity to render truth and inner nature mutable on your own terms. Once out, you don't have quite that degree of capability and to touch it again would be to court Gentrification. That choice makes ripples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T20:18:47-07:00","id":585578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585441#post585441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Essentially, that would make the character Seemingless.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Would it have to, though? A person who is responding to torment and imprisonment in a manner of their choosing is exercising their agency. If they were broken by captivity and simply gave up, resigned themselves to suffering, and did whatever their captor wanted, that would be a loss of agency. But if they remain defiant while they endure (or become defiant after suffering for a time), they are making a choice and determining their own actions within the limited options available to them. It could be taunting their tormentor (&quot;Is that all you've got?&quot;) or simply refusing to cry or scream or notice the torment at all - not giving them the satisfaction. What if the source of this defiance is adopting the stoic strength of granite to endure pain, or if they endure by retreating into an inner world where they focus on their passion, or if they respond to humiliation by abandoning shame and wallowing in depravity? And what if that facilitates their escape, due to their captor becoming bored, or upset, or confused. Wouldn't that earn them a Seeming? I'm genuinely curious. My instinct, if a player brought me a concept like that, would be to say yes. It seems to me like the psychology of the escape, i.e. what they sacrificed/how they changed before their escape and how that sets a foundation for coping with the trauma afterword, is more important to the Seeming than the logistics of the escape itself.<br /> <br /> <i>The Thousand-Eyed Master watched her perform her nauseating task. It's eyes glistened in the torchlight as she cleaned each stone of the kennel floor with her tongue. She worked almost mechanically, seemingly unaware of the stinging cuts all over her body as it splashed another bucket of icy salt water onto her. Its guests grew weary and moved on to other amusements. It cocked one of it's lumpy, malformed heads at the girl. She used to beg and protest, flail and scream, vomit and cry; she used to be entertaining. It assumed she was broken. Her frame was frail and her skin stretched tight over her brittle bones. She must be used up. But it didn't notice that her joints had been soddered back together with strands of shimmering wire, or that her eye had been replaced by a cracked LED screen. It couldn't possibly see the nest of wires, sticks of RAM, and clicking hard drive that resided where her fragile human heart once was. She wasn't really broken, of course; she was just focused on the one thing that mattered - the code for the program she'd been writing, saved in her own precious, perfect memory. It was all she could see, and, strangely, all she could feel. The Thousand-Eyed Master picked up its broken toy and held her close, a moist staccato of blinks echoing in the chamber, and then carried her down the hall like a ragdoll and tossed her onto the trash heap. She'd be long gone before it realized that it had made a mistake.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5910,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","user":"CSSchulz","date":". 07-09-2015, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T20:31:58-07:00","id":585582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585545#post585545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once a thief always a thief. You were born white trash and you'll die white trash.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know you're not actually talking to anyone in particular with this, but man it confused the hell out of me a for a bit. Just wanted that out there.<br /> <br /> @Schulz: You're taking it, but you're not actually <i>doing</i> anything. If a True Fae lets you go because you're boring-well, he still let you go. You made <i>zero</i> choices. You did <i>nothing of merit</i>. Worst of all, <i>you are still taking it</i>.<br /> <br /> Also, retreating into an inner world <i>is exactly what the True Fae do</i>.<br /> <br /> Finally, Endurance is a terrible trait to emphasize on it's own. It's passive, it's background, it just sits there. It's not a proactive trait, it is not the thing that makes <i>protagonists</i>. Going with a brute example, even the characterswho are most marked by their endurance are still people who <i>fucking charge the building</i>. Wolverine is nigh-invulnerable, but I guarentee you never see him just passively taking it when you think of him, and he's just one of several people who <i>start moving forward</i>.<br /> <br /> NOTE: Again, I don't have many hills I will stand and die on. This is one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-09-2015, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T20:51:28-07:00","id":585588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585582#post585582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Schulz: You're taking it, but you're not actually <i>doing</i> anything. If a True Fae lets you go because you're boring-well, he still let you go. You made <i>zero</i> choices. You did <i>nothing of merit</i>. Worst of all, <i>you are still taking it</i>.<br /> <br /> Also, retreating into an inner world <i>is exactly what the True Fae do</i>.<br /> <br /> Finally, Endurance is a terrible trait to emphasize on it's own. It's passive, it's background, it just sits there. It's not a proactive trait, it is not the thing that makes <i>protagonists</i>. Going with a brute example, even the characterswho are most marked by their endurance are still people who <i>fucking charge the building</i>. Wolverine is nigh-invulnerable, but I guarentee you never see him just passively taking it when you think of him, and he's just one of several people who <i>start moving forward</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Defiance is still &quot;doing something&quot;; consider nonviolent protest. You are still making a choice. You're choosing not to give up. Not to give in. If it was on it's own, it would be Seemingless, sure. But I'm talking about Endurance through or because of one of the other Seemings. Your devotion to your craft, denial of self, devotion to others, etc. is what got you through your durance. It might not be the best characteristic for a protagonist, but neither is prudence or fortitude and those are still viable Virtues. On its own, it might not make for a good character, but as one part of a whole character, I think it could be good.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585582#post585582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NOTE: Again, I don't have many hills I will stand and die on. This is one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't trying to convince you. You've already said you won't be convinced. I'm not trying to rile you up. <br /> <br /> I'm not convinced one way or the other myself. I'm just musing out loud. Now, If you want to try and keep convincing me of your point of view, that's fine. I'm open to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5910,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","user":"CSSchulz","date":". 07-10-2015, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T21:04:16-07:00","id":585607,"title":"","content":"... This has been incredibly enlightening. Thank you SO MUCH for this, everyone.<br /> <br /> Though I do wonder - does that mean if you rescue someone from Arcadia, and you're entirely the active party, they're always going to be Seemingless?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T21:09:23-07:00","id":585610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taveena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585607#post585607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... This has been incredibly enlightening. Thank you SO MUCH for this, everyone.<br /> <br /> Though I do wonder - does that mean if you rescue someone from Arcadia, and you're entirely the active party, they're always going to be Seemingless?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like if they were a complete damsel and did nothing to regain their own agency, just waited for rescue? Yeah, I'd say that's a Seemingless character. On the other hand, if they took action and helped themselves escape along with their rescuer, that might be enough to gain a Seeming. Of course, either way it sounds like this story is more about the Fae Touched that's braving Arcadia to find them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T21:19:05-07:00","id":585622,"title":"","content":"By strict interpretation I would say yes, seeming less. As a ST I could see this being a path to fairest, &quot;My loved one risked all to rescue me, inspiring me to do the same&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T21:19:56-07:00","id":585623,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering if there's any advantage to playing a Changeling with no Seeming. Like different xp costs (like VtM Caitiff) to make up for not having affinity Contracts. Maybe some Seemingless-only merits or something. Or maybe they don't have Icons to worry about. All the Seeming descriptions have included the Changeling losing/replacing their heart; maybe having no Seeming means you get to keep your heart. If the number of questions in these threads that get answered with some variation of &quot;well, play a Seemingless Changeling then&quot; is any indication, there are going to be a decent number of folks playing them. Hopefully, we'll find out more soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T21:26:33-07:00","id":585629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585588#post585588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wasn't trying to convince you. You've already said you won't be convinced. I'm not trying to rile you up..</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry. My bad, I got caught up on my hill. This is why I try to avoid them.<br /> <br /> *feels a little bit like a dick now*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T21:55:31-07:00","id":585651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585629#post585629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry. My bad, I got caught up on my hill. This is why I try to avoid them.<br /> <br /> *feels a little bit like a dick now*</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries. I should have made it clear that I was looking for thoughts and feedback from other folks in the thread, since you'd already made your opinion clear. I am new to forum use, so my etiquette may not be the best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T22:52:09-07:00","id":585676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taveena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585607#post585607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... This has been incredibly enlightening. Thank you SO MUCH for this, everyone.<br /> <br /> Though I do wonder - does that mean if you rescue someone from Arcadia, and you're entirely the active party, they're always going to be Seemingless?</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd be very, very hard for your character in question to be the only active party. The other character probably did SOMETHING to make your character want to do that, to put life and limb at risk to save him. But, Seemingless would be the default answer there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T22:56:40-07:00","id":585678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585582#post585582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Schulz: You're taking it, but you're not actually <i>doing</i> anything. If a True Fae lets you go because you're boring-well, he still let you go. You made <i>zero</i> choices. You did <i>nothing of merit</i>. Worst of all, <i>you are still taking it</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Defiance is still &quot;doing something&quot;; consider nonviolent protest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Martin Luther King, Mahatma Gandhi, and Rosa Parks are all prime examples of protagonists who won the day through &quot;passive&quot; means. Rosa literally showed her defiance by sitting still.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585582#post585582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, Endurance is a terrible trait to emphasize on it's own. It's passive, it's background, it just sits there. It's not a proactive trait, it is not the thing that makes <i>protagonists</i>. Going with a brute example, even the characterswho are most marked by their endurance are still people who <i>fucking charge the building</i>. Wolverine is nigh-invulnerable, but I guarentee you never see him just passively taking it when you think of him, and he's just one of several people who <i>start moving forward</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can think of a few times where Wolverine sat there and took a beating, knowing that it wasn't time to strike back yet. There's even a one-off story where he intentionally endures the torments of a concentration camp, in order to we the other prisoners. He was shot, burned, hanged, gassed, etc. He just got back up, day after day, and acted like nothing had happened.<br /> <br /> Also not trying to shove you off your hill. Believe me, I understand what it's like to feel put down, abused, etc., but knowing when to bide your time is just as important as knowing when to lash out and break free. I've made mistakes as to which was which, but I think I'm learning...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 07-10-2015, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T23:35:19-07:00","id":585713,"title":"","content":"Huh. Wolverine's a Wizened.<br /> <br /> Didn't see that one coming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T23:38:15-07:00","id":585714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585713#post585713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. Wolverine's a Wizened.<br /> <br /> Didn't see that one coming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, he is the best there is at what he does!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T00:03:51-07:00","id":585717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585678#post585678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martin Luther King, Mahatma Gandhi, and Rosa Parks are all prime examples of protagonists who won the day through &quot;passive&quot; means. Rosa literally showed her defiance by sitting still.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find classifying these three as &quot;passive&quot; in any sense highly disrespectful to all the proactive things they did (though MLK and Gandhi more prominently than Parks).<br /> <br /> There's a huge gap between passivity and non-violence. The Salt March was not a passive action. It was Gandhi's explicit choice of action despite the dedicated to non-violence. It was a calculated attack on the finances of the British Raj, using a resource necessary for life as a symbol to inspire massive civil disobedience. <br /> <br /> And Rosa Parks didn't show her defiance by sitting still. She was in the aisle seat and moved to the window seat and then didn't move.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Believe me, I understand what it's like to feel put down, abused, etc., but knowing when to bide your time is just as important as knowing when to lash out and break free. </div> </div> </div>I don't think ArcaneArts has an issue with biding your time for the right moment to seize your agency. I believe the metaphorical hill in this case is that biding your time until an external factor tends your situation is the problem. A changeling that simply endures their Durance until someone else frees them doesn't get a Seeming. A changeling that bides their time for the right moment to seize their agency and escape gets one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T00:24:36-07:00","id":585722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585676#post585676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It'd be very, very hard for your character in question to be the only active party. The other character probably did SOMETHING to make your character want to do that, to put life and limb at risk to save him. But, Seemingless would be the default answer there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Fairest...<br /> Who doesn't want to rescue a fair damsel? And, 'sides, you could name her Peach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 07-10-2015, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T00:56:31-07:00","id":585734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585717#post585717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find classifying these three as &quot;passive&quot; in any sense highly disrespectful to all the proactive things they did (though MLK and Gandhi more prominently than Parks).</div> </div> </div> </div>I phrased that incorrectly. What I meant was that all three showed patience, understanding that their goals could not be achieved by acting rashly.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585717#post585717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Rosa Parks didn't show her defiance by sitting still. She was in the aisle seat and moved to the window seat and then didn't move.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, she changed seats, my point was the act of <b>sitting</b> was her defiance.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585717#post585717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think ArcaneArts has an issue with biding your time for the right moment to seize your agency. I believe the metaphorical hill in this case is that biding your time until an external factor tends your situation is the problem. A changeling that simply endures their Durance until someone else frees them doesn't get a Seeming. A changeling that bides their time for the right moment to seize their agency and escape gets one.</div> </div> </div> </div>If rescue arrives before opportunity, does that mean having made your plan is invalidated? My interpretation of the descriptions was that it's what you change about yourself in order to escape, not whether you actually succeed by that change. If a would-be Ogre &quot;Hulks-out&quot;, but fails to break free of that last chain, does that mean he's not an Ogre because 10 minutes later someone else comes along and unlocks it for him? And playing possum, or going for a &quot;Rope-a-Dope&quot; strategy are passive methods, but still take courage to see them through.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T01:11:51-07:00","id":585752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585441#post585441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Essentially, that would make the character Seemingless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may have missed this somewhere, but what does seemingless characters get? No flaws and no blessing or something different?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T01:27:44-07:00","id":585758,"title":"","content":"Basically, yes.<br /> <br /> As Seemings give you both a certain bonus and a certain penalty (wich is a bonus in disguise) you don't get either. You also won't have preferent access to any specific version of a given Contract.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T02:02:34-07:00","id":585779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585717#post585717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a huge gap between passivity and non-violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, but I don't think enduring a durance has to be an inherently passive endeavor. Consider a prisoner of war who suffers physical and psychological torture at the hands of their captors, but never reveals anything beyond name, rank, and service number. Calling that passive would certainly be disrespectful as well. Simply resisting the torture and not giving in to their jailers' demands is an active struggle and an exercise of agency. They may never have an opportunity to break free in the sense you're thinking, but might go through the same psychological and metaphysical changes that grant Changelings a Seeming. And bear in mind that the word escape has multiple definitions, including simply avoiding something (as in &quot;luckily, they escaped serious injury&quot; or <i> to fail to be noticed or recollected by someone</i>. A Changeling who isn't fun to play with anymore because they've learned to ignore the pain and humiliation <i>escapes</i> notice and her Keepers attentions. It may not necessarily have to be in the Shawshank Redemption sense of the word. Again, I'm just musing. Would be nice to get Machine IV's take on this angle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T02:09:41-07:00","id":585781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585734#post585734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I meant was that all three showed patience, understanding that their goals could not be achieved by acting rashly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok... but this has never really been under contention has it? Who's saying that Seemings can't come out of patience and planning?<br /> <br /> The complaint was against the idea that the time spent on enduring a Durance should shape a Seeming rather than the nature of the action that the changeling took to regain agency; not against the idea that some changelings need to wait.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, she changed seats, my point was the act of <b>sitting</b> was her defiance. </div> </div> </div>And we're really just being a bit nitpicky about trying to be clever.<br /> <br /> My counter though, would be the change in words there. The <b>act</b> of sitting (and verbal resistance, and purposefully getting arrested as part of civil disobedience activist movement) is important. Not that she didn't do anything. But that she did something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If rescue arrives before opportunity, does that mean having made your plan is invalidated? </div> </div> </div>Probably? A changeling's plans aren't what determines their Seeming. It's the actions they take. A Darkling might not have planned to betray someone to escape, and the situation went bad leading them to this course of action because they opt to betray and escape rather than risk recapture on the chance they all might escape. If things hadn't gone wrong, they might have come out a Fairest or Wizened as examples.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My interpretation of the descriptions was that it's what you change about yourself in order to escape, not whether you actually succeed by that change. </div> </div> </div>As you don't get a Seeming until you escape, I'm not sure how well that interpretation holds. The descriptions are written from the authorial perspective of telling a compelling narrative example. The details of being taken, the Durance, and the escape as a Seeming all flowing into each other in a logical narrative flow. But claiming a Seeming happens at the end of the process, and it can change based on how that process ends.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a would-be Ogre &quot;Hulks-out&quot;, but fails to break free of that last chain, does that mean he's not an Ogre because 10 minutes later someone else comes along and unlocks it for him? </div> </div> </div>He's not an Ogre until he completely escapes. He wasn't an Ogre just for trying to break free in an Ogre-type fashion, because he hasn't achieving &quot;Seeming-hood&quot; yet. His Seeming isn't changing back and forth during all this. It's the end result of the escape. He might retain being an Ogre after fully escaping, become Seemingless as someone supplants his agency by freeing him before he can fully assert it, or he might end up a different Seeming despite being on a path to be an Ogre as the situation changes beyond his control and he needs to find a new method of reclaiming that control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And playing possum, or going for a &quot;Rope-a-Dope&quot; strategy are passive methods, but still take courage to see them through. </div> </div> </div>Possibly. Though again, I'm not seeing where this comes in. Biding time doesn't seem to be an issue unless it's all you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T02:26:40-07:00","id":585794,"title":"","content":"I guess what I'm trying to say is that the choice to take no action(physically) <i>is</i> still a choice, which is still exercising one's agency, and can lead to escape. Elemental: Remain as still as a stone, until your Keeper gets bored and moves on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T06:32:46-07:00","id":585992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585610#post585610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like if they were a complete damsel and did nothing to regain their own agency, just waited for rescue?</div> </div> </div> </div>One really cool escape I've been keeping in mind is intentionally acting like the most steryotypical damsel imagineable and useing that to talecraft-summon a knight to rescue you. That would most probably result in a Wizened if you treat Talecrafting as the Wizened's craft. Alternatively a Darkling or a Fairest are both possible, depending on how you treat the knight afterwords (assuming there's enough adventure between your prison and the exit)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T07:12:07-07:00","id":586059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585717#post585717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find classifying these three as &quot;passive&quot; in any sense highly disrespectful to all the proactive things they did (though MLK and Gandhi more prominently than Parks).<br /> <br /> There's a huge gap between passivity and non-violence. The Salt March was not a passive action. It was Gandhi's explicit choice of action despite the dedicated to non-violence. It was a calculated attack on the finances of the British Raj, using a resource necessary for life as a symbol to inspire massive civil disobedience.<br /> <br /> And Rosa Parks didn't show her defiance by sitting still. She was in the aisle seat and moved to the window seat and then didn't move.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't think ArcaneArts has an issue with biding your time for the right moment to seize your agency. I believe the metaphorical hill in this case is that biding your time until an external factor tends your situation is the problem. A changeling that simply endures their Durance until someone else frees them doesn't get a Seeming. A changeling that bides their time for the right moment to seize their agency and escape gets one.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, Everything here, I love, I approve. Same with everything else Arms has said here.<br /> <br /> Second, I had a misunderstanding, I removed it.<br /> <br /> Third, Can we just take a second to say Rose Parks is always a weird one to bring up? Just want to say that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-10-2015, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T07:27:38-07:00","id":586067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=585992#post585992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One really cool escape I've been keeping in mind is intentionally acting like the most steryotypical damsel imagineable and useing that to talecraft-summon a knight to rescue you. That would most probably result in a Wizened if you treat Talecrafting as the Wizened's craft. Alternatively a Darkling or a Fairest are both possible, depending on how you treat the knight afterwords (assuming there's enough adventure between your prison and the exit)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an awesome idea!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T07:34:24-07:00","id":586077,"title":"","content":"I'm really hoping there will be a damsel in distress Kith. I think MachineIV said he'll try to sneak one into Dark Eras; and if not I'll just homebrew one for everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T07:36:18-07:00","id":586078,"title":"","content":"Gotta admit, I do like that Raven. Be a hell of an excuse for a Retainer coming out of the Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T09:10:04-07:00","id":586198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=586077#post586077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really hoping there will be a damsel in distress Kith. I think MachineIV said he'll try to sneak one into Dark Eras; and if not I'll just homebrew one for everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dark Eras Seeming will definitely do Damsel in Distress. Not just that. But definitely that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T10:43:58-07:00","id":586257,"title":"","content":"Awesome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T13:10:38-07:00","id":586406,"title":"","content":"The tale crafting idea could fit for all of the seemings if you think about it, your seeming and even your successful escape are based on following an appropriate narrative. The ogre breaks his chains, the darkling slips through a crack, a story with classic elements played out in a realm that shapes to fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T06:19:49-07:00","id":587013,"title":"","content":"To me, regaining agency doesn't necessarily mean escaping. Agency is a much more personal thing than your physical freedom. It's the moment that you decide that they don't own you anymore, or that they can't hurt you again. Sure, you might still be physically in their dungeon, but mentally your are wild and free. <br /> <br /> Let's look at the Genie from Aladdin. Does he get a Seeming? I'd say yes. But not from when Al says &quot;Genie, I wish you free.&quot; I'd say it happens during the fight before Iago steals the lamp, when the Genie calls Aladdin out on his BS for not keeping his promise. That's when Genie becomes a Beast for breaking the social convention of slaves not talking back, the rest is just paperwork.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T06:28:08-07:00","id":587015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andreamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=587013#post587013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, regaining agency doesn't necessarily mean escaping. Agency is a much more personal thing than your physical freedom. It's the moment that you decide that they don't own you anymore, or that they can't hurt you again. Sure, you might still be physically in their dungeon, but mentally your are wild and free.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but we're talking about Arcadia, where there is no distinction between the symbolic and the literal. By reclaiming agency snd therefore gaining symbolic freedom, you become literally, physically free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T14:33:28-07:00","id":587443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=587015#post587015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but we're talking about Arcadia, where there is no distinction between the symbolic and the literal. By reclaiming agency snd therefore gaining symbolic freedom, you become literally, physically free.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! So, if someone were to become immune to their Keeper's torments through a mind over matter approach or sheer force of will, that metaphorical escape would manifest as a literal escape? So, if they're escaping into their music, they might find a trail of sheet music into a tunnel that leads them to safety (Wizened). Or if they adopt the unfeeling nature of stone to endure torture, they literally become one with the land and can pull themselves out of the earth in the hedge (Elemental). Or, maybe, they withstand horrible torture and refuse to rat out their fellow prisoners, so then the Wyrd causes their guards to drop the key just within reach of his cell door (Fairest). Technically, they're not <i>doing</i> anything different than someone who's toughing it out - endurance/fortitude/willpower is still the thrust of it, but the Wyrd makes it into a literal &quot;breaking out&quot; sort of escape. Their internal resistance is transformed into an external means of gaining freedom. I can get behind this. I feel like I can easily modify players' concepts if something like this comes up, with this in mind. So, thanks for that, Charlaquin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T15:04:08-07:00","id":587451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=587015#post587015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but we're talking about Arcadia, where there is no distinction between the symbolic and the literal. By reclaiming agency snd therefore gaining symbolic freedom, you become literally, physically free.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure it doesn't quite work that way. Take an Fairest, you can inspire the slaves to rebel. Lead your army against the keeper's guards, and get soundly defeated.<br /> <br /> Also, I think Arcadia has a ton of distinction between the symbolic and the literal. Mage &amp; the Supernal realm is the place where symbols and reality are one. Arcadia isn't symbology (unless you say it's the Supernal Arcadia), it's stories. If you open a, lets say a Dresden Files book, it's easy to distinguish between symbology and literal truth in the context of the story.<br /> <br /> Which is I think for the best. If it was purely a case of reclaiming agency makes you free, then the Keeper's influence becomes negligible. It doesn't matter if the keeper threw you into the arena or into the mines; only your personal charachter development matters. That's a bit too solipsistic for my tastes and downplaying the Keeper is downplaying a powerful antagonistic relationship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T15:16:02-07:00","id":587462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=587451#post587451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure it doesn't quite work that way. Take an Fairest, you can inspire the slaves to rebel. Lead your army against the keeper's guards, and get soundly defeated.<br /> <br /> Also, I think Arcadia has a ton of distinction between the symbolic and the literal. Mage &amp; the Supernal realm is the place where symbols and reality are one. Arcadia isn't symbology (unless you say it's the Supernal Arcadia), it's stories. If you open a, lets say a Dresden Files book, it's easy to distinguish between symbology and literal truth in the context of the story.<br /> <br /> Which is I think for the best. If it was purely a case of reclaiming agency makes you free, then the Keeper's influence becomes negligible. It doesn't matter if the keeper threw you into the arena or into the mines; only your personal charachter development matters. That's a bit too solipsistic for my tastes and downplaying the Keeper is downplaying a powerful antagonistic relationship.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's more about reclaiming agency giving you an <i>opportunity</i>. It nudges the story in a certain direction. You could still fail, but the Wyrd grants you a chance, even if it's a slim one, as a sort of response to your agency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5910,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","user":"CSSchulz","date":". 07-11-2015, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T15:17:55-07:00","id":587463,"title":"","content":"So having a moment that makes you more like the Keeper(by indulging in solipsism) while denying it more power is not to your taste?<br /> <br /> Also, maybe you missed the part where your Kith comes from them? And if anything it emphasizes the antagonistic relationship between the two, because now what you do to defy them <i>fucking matters</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T15:47:33-07:00","id":587472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=587462#post587462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's more about reclaiming agency giving you an <i>opportunity</i>. It nudges the story in a certain direction. You could still fail, but the Wyrd grants you a chance, even if it's a slim one, as a sort of response to your agency.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more that you can't escape without excercising agency by definition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=587463#post587463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So having a moment that makes you more like the Keeper(by indulging in solipsism) while denying it more power is not to your taste?</div> </div> </div> </div> Correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=587463#post587463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if anything it emphasizes the antagonistic relationship between the two, because now what you do to defy them <i>fucking matters</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>How you defy them matters either way.<br /> <br /> It's the significance of everything else that's in question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T17:43:15-07:00","id":587569,"title":"","content":"I feel it's worth pointing out that the endurance-based archetype of escape is more Ogrish than Elemental.<br /> <br /> A metaphor I remember stumbling on back in 1e when these were chiefly aesthetic differences concerns the titular creatures in Shadow of the Colossus \u2014 if things are growing on an earthy Ogre, it's because she doesn't care about them. Meanwhile, if things <i>aren't</i> growing on an earthy Elemental, it's because she doesn't care about them.<br /> <br /> The land is not the landslide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-11-2015, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T20:10:44-07:00","id":587657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=587569#post587569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel it's worth pointing out that the endurance-based archetype of escape is more Ogrish than Elemental.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. The Seeming write up for the 2e Ogre explicitly mentions biding their time and becoming inured to pain. But the Seeming is also characterized by a violent, destructive escape. I, for one, was wondering more about how a durance based around endurance could lead to freedom without going the violent route, ending with a different Seeming. And I'm curious what &quot;counts&quot; as a Seeming-forging escape, since the examples are fairly vague and seem like they leave a lot of wiggle room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T21:16:18-07:00","id":587687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=587657#post587657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. The Seeming write up for the 2e Ogre explicitly mentions biding their time and becoming inured to pain. But the Seeming is also characterized by a violent, destructive escape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arcadia is ringed with Thorns and immunity to pain presents an exceedingly straightforward way to get past that.<br /> <br /> It might be more accurate to say that the Ogrish escape is about cultivated insensitivity and that hooks into a significant chunk of the splat's associated stereotypes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I, for one, was wondering more about how a durance based around endurance could lead to freedom without going the violent route, ending with a different Seeming. </div> </div> </div>The fact that &quot;endurance&quot; contains the word &quot;durance&quot; is not an etymological accident. We're talking about Arcadia here \u2014 <i>everyone</i> with a means of escape is biding their time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T22:11:10-07:00","id":587708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=587687#post587687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arcadia is ringed with Thorns and immunity to pain presents an exceedingly straightforward way to get past that.<br /> <br /> It might be more accurate to say that the Ogrish escape is about cultivated insensitivity and that hooks into a significant chunk of the splat's associated stereotypes.<br /> <br /> The fact that &amp;quot;endurance&amp;quot; contains the word &amp;quot;durance&amp;quot; is not an etymological accident. We're talking about Arcadia here \u2014 <i>everyone</i> with a means of escape is biding their time.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, are you saying the Ogre's escape doesn't have to be violent? The bits about destroying everything in their wake, brutality, and chaos made me think it was a necessary facet, especially given their blessing. Would someone who fit the Ogre description (toughening up, biding their time, becoming emotionally nigh invulnerable), but escaped in some nonviolent way be an Ogre or have no Seeming? If they had no Seeming, would they still look kind of like an Ogre?<br /> <br /> Everybody who's still in good enough shape to be able to escape has endured. That certainly makes sense. Good point. I think I was focusing too much on scenarios where a character endures in a manner that's consistent with a Seeming, but ends up getting released because they endured or lasts long enough to get rescued.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T22:53:42-07:00","id":587717,"title":"","content":"I think endurance could be part of any Seeming's escape, but I don't think endurance alone is enough to gain a Seeming. You need to take your story into your own hands, claim your agency, forge your own destiny, make your escape. Take, claim, forge, and make are all active verbs. You have to <i>do</i> something to gain a Seeming. Biding your time can certainly be part of what you do, but if you're not an active participant in gaining your own freedom, that's not agency. That's accepting your lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T00:02:05-07:00","id":587876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=587717#post587717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think endurance could be part of any Seeming's escape, but I don't think endurance alone is enough to gain a Seeming. You need to take your story into your own hands, claim your agency, forge your own destiny, make your escape. Take, claim, forge, and make are all active verbs. You have to <i>do</i> something to gain a Seeming. Biding your time can certainly be part of what you do, but if you're not an active participant in gaining your own freedom, that's not agency. That's accepting your lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly my point. Thank you.<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that the Ogres and Elementals(and the Wizened to some degree) make mention of the use of endurance in the process of their escape, but it's not the whole of it-the embrace of the violence, the surrender of ego to one's place in the world, the becoming of the craft, these are the shifts in being that allow of perspective and power for one to defy the world.<br /> <br /> And part of the reason why I gently mocked Raven's argument about solipsism is because, let's be honest, in order to escape, you have to decide you are more important than the world you are currently in. A Seeming is declarative in a similar manner to Mummy's Decrees, that you are, for whatever newfound virtue/vice you've discovered, substantially more, bigger, more valuable to the whole of existence than the world you are in. Your actions and perspectives justify the mean and shape your character. Even an Elemental's revelation that they aren't the most important thing in the universe fills them with a perspective bigger than the True Fae they dwell in, because by virtue of declaring themselves a small drop in the ocean, they simultaneously declare the True Fae as equally small, and their clarity of place in the vast world makers them wiser, more observant than them-bigger, more substantial, more mature, and therefore worthier of powerful agency than their captors. Narratives of any sort respond this sort of shift in character-it's the culmination of a character arc, the change in chapters or stories. Thus, a changeling who follows a Seeming's route and succeeds courts both physical actuality and narrative catharsis of the moment-the changeling's Seeming declaration makes them, for a moment, narratively larger and more important than the True Fae, and thus lays out more story elements to facilitate the changing narrative, in a &quot;fortune favors the bold/fate helps those who help themselves&quot; sort of way. And this all works because of the Wyrd's nature as a connective tidal force of pretty much everything, as a thing that changes recurrences into tropes and transforms them into vehicles of meaning.<br /> <br /> So let me put it this way-endurance matters as a cauldron for the collection of narrative potential energy, the buildup to the climax of one story. The Seeming is the Climax, the culmination of everything that is affecting the character that leads to their first milestone actualization, and the Escape is the resolution and bridge to the next story, the one that you'll be playing in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-12-2015, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T00:17:57-07:00","id":587894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=587708#post587708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, are you saying the Ogre's escape doesn't have to be violent?</div> </div> </div> </div> An Ogre decides that their softer emotions, compassion, empathy, etc, are a weakness and so they cut out their heart to remove them.<br /> <br /> Violence makes sense after that - if compassion is holding you back then it's probably holding you back from hurting someone - but violence isn't strictly required.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for endurance; all Seemings need that. If you don't have endurance you won't live long enough to escape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T00:25:41-07:00","id":587898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=587876#post587876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even an Elemental's revelation that they aren't the most important thing in the universe fills them with a perspective bigger than the True Fae they dwell in, because by virtue of declaring themselves a small drop in the ocean, they simultaneously declare the True Fae as equally small, and their clarity of place in the vast world makers them wiser, more observant than them-bigger, more substantial, more mature, and therefore worthier of powerful agency than their captors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've recently noted that a valid way of framing the Elemental escape is that by immersing yourself in the nature of your kith, <i>reality ensues</i> \u2014 the fire or the river or the storm or whatever is no longer constrained by the bonds of your ego and proceeds to <i>do what that element does</i>, goblin scripting be damned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T00:27:15-07:00","id":587901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=587898#post587898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've recently noted that a valid way of framing the Elemental escape is that by immersing yourself in the nature of your kith, <i>reality ensues</i> \u2014 the fire or the river or the storm or whatever is no longer constrained by the bonds of your ego and proceeds to <i>do what that element does</i>, goblin scripting be damned.</div> </div> </div> </div>That moment when you both realize reality is larger than both of you and is going to beat up one of you for your lunch money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-06-2015, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T00:36:18-07:00","id":587904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=587876#post587876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And part of the reason why I gently mocked Raven's argument about solipsism is because, let's be honest, in order to escape, you have to decide you are more important than the world you are currently in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. But that's pretty much tangenical to what I was saying about solipsism.<br /> <br /> In essence I was saying that the escape had to make sense as a narrative, cos you know, Arcadia is built on stories.<br /> <br /> It's not enough for Weedy McWimp to emotionally and mentally reach the stage of ripping out his heart and becoming an Ogre then fighting his way to freedom because heart or no heart it doesn't make sense for Weedy McWimp to beat guards in a fight.<br /> <br /> Now if his durance taught Weedy McWimp how to fight before he ripped out his heart, that's another story. Otherwise, he'd be best off using his actual skills to escape. Maybe a childhood hiding from bullies gives him a high Stealth score.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=587876#post587876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Narratives of any sort respond this sort of shift in character-it's the culmination of a character arc, the change in chapters or stories. Thus, a changeling who follows a Seeming's route and succeeds courts both physical actuality and narrative catharsis of the moment-the changeling's Seeming declaration makes them, for a moment, narratively larger and more important than the True Fae</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the key thing to remember, is that the Changeling starts out as a bit charachter in the True Fae's story. When you say the narrative responds to this sort of shift; typically it only does so for major and secondary characters.<br /> <br /> A Changeling isn't an important charachter. They're a bit charachter in their Keeper's story, who's trying to become the protagonist of their own story. Or to put it differently. When the protagonist reaches the culmination of their charachter ark they're following the narrative. When a Changeling reaches the culimnation of their Durance charachter arc they're not following the narrative, they're trying to hijack the narrative.<br /> <br /> Thus, the narrative A.K.A. the True Fae is going to fight back.<br /> <br /> That's why I say it's important that the Changeling's escape plan works on a practical level. And why Weedy McWimp should try to sneak out rather than fight. Weedy McWimp getting combat skill out of nowhere is a weak narrative with little internal consistency; and when his weak narrative fights the True Fae's strong narrative it looses. Weedy's narrative loosing manifests in Arcadia as the guards defeating him in combat.<br /> <br /> But if Weedy McWimp using an escape plan that makes sense given his personality, his skills, and the defences the True Fae created to prevent escapes; thats a strong narrative that can fight the True Fae's narrative and win.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-12-2015, 03:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T00:41:56-07:00","id":587907,"title":"","content":"Given some of your other arguments on the subject of Seemings, I am utterly confused as to your position.<br /> <br /> I'd go into more, but I have a website to make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T01:22:12-07:00","id":587922,"title":"","content":"... This is a bit tricky, but... to be entirely honest, I don't entirely understand what the Ogre DOES to escape. Or rather, what defines an escape route as an Ogre rather than another Seeming.<br /> <br /> Possibly because I'm kinda terrible with... what SEEMS to be simile (i mean, I assume it is, because I doubt EVERY ogre literally rips out their own heart). Is it the rampage of their escape, or... the... whatever the 'pulls their own heart out' means?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T01:27:33-07:00","id":587923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=587907#post587907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given some of your other arguments on the subject of Seemings, I am utterly confused as to your position.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ok, if you ever want to ask me about it I'm right here.<br /> <br /> <br /> Though I think I can guess why you're confused. Is it because I just wrote a post arguing for more backstory tie in when I've previously been saying that there's too much backstory?<br /> <br /> If so. There's a simple and consistant reason. My position has always been that how you escape should be a coherent story that makes sense given <b>both</b> your backstory and the threats and challenges that face you in your durance.<br /> <br /> Since my position is essentially in the middle I can argue for more backstory if I feel there's not enough; for example Weedy McWimp winning a fight strikes me as ignoring large parts of his backstory, specifically the part about him being crap at fighting. But I can also argue for less backstory if I feel there's too much; for example the Wizened write up made me feel* that an autistic computer programmer would use his computer skills and to me that's too much focus on backstory because it ignores the possibility of him ending up in a Durance where computers don't exist.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Yes I know that this isn't the intent; but that doesn't change the way I feel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taveena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=587922#post587922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... This is a bit tricky, but... to be entirely honest, I don't entirely understand what the Ogre DOES to escape. Or rather, what defines an escape route as an Ogre rather than another Seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the &quot;whatever the 'pulls their own heart out' means?&quot; that makes an Ogre.<br /> <br /> An Ogre decides that if they want to escape, they have to be metaphorically 'heartless'. But why must they be heartless, there must be thousands of reasons.<br /> <br /> An Ogre might fight his way through the guards; if he has sympathy and compassion for his foes he'd fight slower - thus he must be heartless.<br /> An Ogre might be enslaved as a spouse to his keeper. He can leave at any time, but he loves them too much - thus he must be heartless.<br /> An Ogre might know how to build a flying machine and escape, but all the trees are alive and beg him when he starts to chop wood - thus he must be heartless. (Note how close this escape is to a Wizened - it easily could go either way)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-12-2015, 04:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T02:28:55-07:00","id":587976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=587717#post587717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Biding your time can certainly be part of what you do, but if you're not an active participant in gaining your own freedom, that's not agency. That's accepting your lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the part I disagree with you on. A character could constantly think about escape, the hope of escape could be what keeps them going, they could even make multiple attempts, but they never have the opportunity to escape, or when the opportunity comes they could be physically incapable because of what they've suffered, or they could simply fail. They might still be rescued or released and gain freedom without being an active participant of their actual escape. It <i>may</i> be true that they lacked agency as a character (probably more accurately, that they were robbed of agency).* But it <i>doesn't</i> mean that they're accepting their lot. This is often the case in real life. People often <i>can't</i> get out of those sorts of situations on their own, or actively participate in gaining their freedom, but that doesn't necessarily mean that they've given up, surrendered, or accepted their lot. Now, when you say that, in Arcadia, the Wyrd would manufacture an opportunity for them to escape or grant them the strength despite any injuries or impediments they've suffered, I can totally get behind that. If the Wyrd opens the door (and makes sure their legs work when it does), then it's their job to walk through it.<br /> <br /> *T<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">hat depends on how you define agency, and it's a tricky term - I haven't been able to find a single, widely-accepted definition for the use of it as it applies to fictional characters. (To me, so long as they are trying to escape, struggling to endure, and/or refusing to be broken, they have agency.)</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5910,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","user":"CSSchulz","date":". 07-12-2015, 05:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T03:45:56-07:00","id":588004,"title":"","content":"Such a charachter would, in my opinion, most like end up with no Seeming. When Seeming says &quot;how you regain agency&quot;, I always read that as having an implicit 'successfully' in there. So failed escape attempts don't count. Nor do I think the Wyrd would manufacture an opportunity for them to escape, it's far more awesome and keeping with the theme of reclaiming agency if Changelings have to go look for oppotunities themselves.<br /> <br /> Now that said, I don't think you'll get many cases where a someone would have several failed escape attempts followed by being rescued and having no seeming. Once the knight rescues you from the tower there's still everything else between you and the edge of Arcadia. That's plenty of opportunities to do something that gives you a Seeming.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T04:30:13-07:00","id":588014,"title":"","content":"It's not a moment of actualization if you don't actualize anything. Success is the culminating point, the point and proof of becoming.<br /> <br /> Now, how much of that is the character and how much of that is the Wyrd is something PC's should wonder and worry about. Did they make the choice freely, or are their lives scripted more than they think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T04:59:45-07:00","id":588025,"title":"","content":"Now that I agree with. While I lean heavily towards it being the charachter; I also agree that Changelings can't say for sure. It's all a big trick by their Keeper for all they know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T05:52:30-07:00","id":588047,"title":"","content":"I like to think of it leaning towards the character, with a mention that the character who is building up to a Seeming acts on the Wyrd like the moon pulling on the tides-a character builds their own narrative mass as they reclaim their agency, and correspondingly build their own fate. So yes, the Wyrd helps, but it's because of the character seizing their own fate.<br /> <br /> Were I to write in in a book, though, I'd definitely just leave it nebulous what exactly happens there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T06:38:12-07:00","id":588098,"title":"","content":"The Wyrd definately helps, but it also hinders because the True Fae have their narrative too and their narrative says you're an unimportant bit charachter.<br /> <br /> Hence why Weedy McWimp can't just rip his heart out and fight his way to freedom. As he works his way towards Ogre he will pull in Wyrd and build up a narrative mass. It just won't be a strong enough narrative to overwrite the True Fae's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T07:32:08-07:00","id":588116,"title":"","content":"It doesn't necessarily need to. Building your narrative doesn't mean you overwrite another you were already a part of, especially if you were just a side character in that one. It's a bit like writing a spin-off.<br /> <br /> Taking your agency back from the Keeper is rewriting your own narrative and taking control of it. But unless it was a vital part of the Keeper's, as opposed to a footnote or minor role, then you do not need to overpower them to actualize it. You just need to wrench a small part of the True Fae's story so it can be /your/ story again.<br /> <br /> At least, that's how I see it. Not to say every attempt at reclaiming agency will be successful, but it's more responsive to the effort and personal development involved than one might think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-12-2015, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T08:15:41-07:00","id":588148,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what the difference between what I said and &quot;You just need to wrench a small part of the True Fae's story so it can be /your/ story again.&quot; is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T08:50:26-07:00","id":588171,"title":"","content":"In addition to Yolf's comment, I just want to point out that changeling's also have the weight of their own lives which have more substance than a True Fae's. When a True Fae declares &quot;I AM&quot; to the universe, that's the beginning of their life- Arcadia is pretty much the whole of it. When a changeling declares 'I AM&quot;, there's that weight of reality fitting it like rebar in concrete, or a rock at the heart of a snowball.<br /> <br /> How much that matters is up to the individual again, but I like to think it's also substantial.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of factors that go into a Changeling's metaphysical make-up in my head, I freely admit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-12-2015, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T09:10:45-07:00","id":588206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=588148#post588148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what the difference between what I said and &quot;You just need to wrench a small part of the True Fae's story so it can be /your/ story again.&quot; is.</div> </div> </div> </div>The resistance posed by the Keeper. The same difference between a character taking over the main role and making a spin-off of their own.<br /> <br /> What Arc pointed out is also relevant. In my view, there are important, fundamental differences between changelings and the gentry that might mark the former as more genuine, for lack of a better word.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-12-2015, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T11:31:41-07:00","id":588329,"title":"","content":"I'm just going to say, all it took for Sarah to escape the Labyrinth was to say, &quot;you have no power over me&quot; and mean it. All Dorothy had to do to leave Oz was click her heels together and say &quot;there's no place like home.&quot; All Alice had to do to wake up from her dream of Wonderland was to tell the court they were all just a silly pack of cards. <br /> <br /> They all had to go through an ordeal in their respective Arcadias to find the strength to make those declarations, but it was within them all along, they just didn't know it, and it took a journey to show them their own power.<br /> <br /> That's what I think a Changeling's escape should be. Yes, they rebel or betray or lead or fight or let go or better themselves as part of their journey of self-actualization. But the actual moment of escape is the moment when they declare that they are stronger than their captors and they will not be held back any longer. Everything before that moment is just part of the learning process they had to go through to reach that point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T11:41:04-07:00","id":588335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=588098#post588098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wyrd definately helps, but it also hinders because the True Fae have their narrative too and their narrative says you're an unimportant bit charachter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would actually argue the opposite point. The stories of the True Fae thrive on conflict and opposition, at least in 1e; one of the Gentry who exists in opposition is one whose story will soon enough wither and die. I recall some line to the effect of two Strangers who are bitter enemies being about as close to besties as they can get, because they both provide an endless avenue of conflict for each others' tales. From the perspective of a True Fae, it's to the <i>benefit</i> of their narratives that an unimportant bit character become so elevated. It's a plot twist that gives them a new and personal avenue for conflict. Perhaps it hurts a bit in the short run, but can ultimately be much more advantageous to them.<br /> <br /> I could honestly see that the True Fae might themselves not want this, but the Wyrd certainly does. It wants the stories of the world to be interesting. And what's interesting about the Changeling being an unimportant bit character? There's nothing there. No conflict, no growth, a complete narrative dead-end. But when the Changeling gives up something of significance in pursuit of a Seeming? There's a fine narrative seed to be nurtured, there. Far more valuable than what was previously a stale bit of crust on a Stranger's story. I have this image of a time-lapse film with a sprouting plant swallowing or tearing apart an unmoving rock. It's not about overpowering the True Fae's narrative, not completely -- which could instead be expressed by actually wiping the Stranger out. It's about overpowering it in a place and manner in which it is vulnerable.<br /> <br /> As to the point of the Changeling's being a weaker story, that's not really a determination one can make just by describing what happened. Two different stories can have the exact same events, but the respective framing and telling of those stories can make the difference. One may be dull as dishwater while the other is absolutely edge-of-your-seat level compelling. &quot;Someone truly giving up a significant part of herself in pursuit of freedom,&quot; is kind of tricky to <i>not</i> make an interesting and significant personal development, and it can be the seed of a fascinating story. Never mind that it fits the Wyrd's notion of bargaining, agreements, and give-and-take to a T.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Cleaning up a smidge, and rephrasing ab it. 07-12-2015, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T12:09:06-07:00","id":588382,"title":"","content":"I would also like to note, in support of my thoughts that the Changeling seizes freedom by making their own narrative and escaping from the likely diminute role their Keeper placed them in; and in following the argument that there are some fundamental differences between the Lost and the Gentry that affect the responsiveness of the Wyrd to their respective metaphysical declaration of existence and individuality (as Arc noted in his last comment); Changelings can create. The True Fae can't, not truly.<br /> <br /> To validate their self, the True Fae must draw on existing narratives, bonds and stories, fabricating them in imitation of a dynamic whole, deliberately working to cause conflict in which they have a part, and sublimate other things to build up their own importance as vital and superior to them. Changelings, and indeed humans, do not require this. They are grounded in reality and possess a spark of originality and imagination, of true and new potential that allows them to create a unique narrative just by living.<br /> <br /> The Others need to justify their mercurial being existing as separate from the Wyrd. Changelings do not, and are all the more real for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-12-2015, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T12:22:48-07:00","id":588391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=588335#post588335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would actually argue the opposite point. The stories of the True Fae thrive on conflict and opposition, at least in 1e; one of the Gentry who exists in opposition is one whose story will soon enough wither and die.</div> </div> </div> </div> To respond to this I need only point out that it's actually: &quot;The stories of the True Fae thrive on conflict and opposition where <b>the True Fae wins</b>&quot;.<br /> <br /> Obviously a Changeling escaping doesn't hurt them like another True Fae winning would - they don't loose a Title to every Changeling - but I think it's fair to say that the True Fae benefit more from a dramatic escape attempt that fails than from a dramtic escape attempt that succeedes. If nothing else, the Changeling will likely try again and thus you get two neat stories.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=588335#post588335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what's interesting about the Changeling being an unimportant bit character? There's nothing there. No conflict, no growth, a complete narrative dead-end. But when the Changeling gives up something of significance in pursuit of a Seeming? There's a fine narrative seed to be nurtured, there.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ah, but you must ask yourself who are the main charachters?<br /> <br /> The main charachter could be another True Fae or perhaps a rare and (un)lucky changeling. Stories are like pyramids. You have a few important charachters, and lots and lots of unimportant charachters, especially if you count the nameless armies or crowd scenes.<br /> <br /> A Changeling might be more potent in an important role, but if all those roles are filled already to the minor roles they go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=588335#post588335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Someone truly giving up a significant part of herself in pursuit of freedom,&quot; is kind of tricky to <i>not</i> make an interesting and significant personal development, .</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the moment you said this I can think of a great counter example: The origonal ending to Fallout III.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You need to go into a radioactive room and press The Button. You can't send in the radiation proof robot. You can't send in the radiation proof supermutant. You can't use all those anti-rad drugs in your inventory.<br /> <br /> Nope, either you or one other party member has to die.<br /> <br /> Players didn't think that was an interesting and significant personal development. They just thought it was stupid.<br /> <br /> Same for Changelings. If their escape attempt makes little sense, it's a poor story and won't overcome the True Fae's story.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T12:42:17-07:00","id":588397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=588391#post588391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think it's fair to say that the True Fae benefit more from a dramatic escape attempt that fails than from a dramtic escape attempt that succeedes.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is not even remotely true. A changeling that tries to escape but fails will be an afternoon's entertainment. They might try again once or twice, but eventually they're just going to accept their fate. <br /> <br /> One who <i>succeeds</i> on the other hand, well, they're emboldened by the experience. They become a foe, a constant source of antagonism that stays elusively out of reach. And, given time, they can grow in power and hatch into a fae themselves, and then they'll provide some <i>real</i> opposition. <br /> <br /> In the long term, an escaped changeling is <i>infinitely</i> more beneficial than one that remains a loyal pet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T14:19:21-07:00","id":588480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=588397#post588397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One who <i>succeeds</i> on the other hand, well, they're emboldened by the experience. They become a foe, a constant source of antagonism that stays elusively out of reach. And, given time, they can grow in power and hatch into a fae themselves, and then they'll provide some <i>real</i> opposition.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they wont. 9 times out 10 they'll do anything to avoid antagonising or attracting attention to their former Keeper.<br /> <br /> (Plus it really takes away from the whole reclaiming agency theme if half the reason you escaped is that Keepers want Changelings to escape)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T14:56:36-07:00","id":588498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=588329#post588329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just going to say, all it took for Sarah to escape the Labyrinth was to say, &quot;you have no power over me&quot; and mean it. All Dorothy had to do to leave Oz was click her heels together and say &quot;there's no place like home.&quot; All Alice had to do to wake up from her dream of Wonderland was to tell the court they were all just a silly pack of cards.<br /> <br /> They all had to go through an ordeal in their respective Arcadias to find the strength to make those declarations, but it was within them all along, they just didn't know it, and it took a journey to show them their own power.<br /> <br /> That's what I think a Changeling's escape should be. Yes, they rebel or betray or lead or fight or let go or better themselves as part of their journey of self-actualization. But the actual moment of escape is the moment when they declare that they are stronger than their captors and they will not be held back any longer. Everything before that moment is just part of the learning process they had to go through to reach that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stuff like this makes me want to write a campaign about being captured and becoming a changeling rather than playing after the fact. Alice in Wonderland style of shit going on, everything is crazy and dangerous and unknown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T15:02:51-07:00","id":588502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=588498#post588498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stuff like this makes me want to write a campaign about being captured and becoming a changeling rather than playing after the fact. Alice in Wonderland style of shit going on, everything is crazy and dangerous and unknown.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of what's so cool about Changeling though is its like the second act of Into the Woods. It shows the aftermath of those stories. It asks what happened to Alice after she got back from Wonderland, and in doing so deconstructs the genre. Don't get me wrong, I think a story where you start out with human characters and play through their capture and their durance, culminating in the escape and gaining a Seeming would be a blast. But I think the story of what happens after that is a bit more appropriate for the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> I would also love to run or play in a Fae-Touched game, where you're going into the hedge to try to save a taken loved one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T15:37:38-07:00","id":588516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=588480#post588480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No they wont. 9 times out 10 they'll do anything to avoid antagonising or attracting attention to their former Keeper.<br /> <br /> (Plus it really takes away from the whole reclaiming agency theme if half the reason you escaped is that Keepers want Changelings to escape)</div> </div> </div> </div>But the <i>tenth</i>? Oh, my, they more than make up for it.<br /> <br /> And just because the Fae <i>want </i> you to escape doesn't mean they'll just <i>let</i> you. That would defeat the point. They <i>need</i> you to <i>genuinely</i> reclaim your agency. That's how it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 07-12-2015, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T18:14:33-07:00","id":588635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=587708#post587708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, are you saying the Ogre's escape doesn't have to be violent? The bits about destroying everything in their wake, brutality, and chaos made me think it was a necessary facet, especially given their blessing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a changeling who has made themselves into a big dumb blunt mass of careless unfeeling scar tissue in the midst of a notable number of significant obstacles that led the changeling to conclude the development of those traits was necessary \u2014 the Ogres are the most literal about their escape breaking things, which is kind of hard to do on a dramatic timescale without some degree of violence.<br /> <br /> <i>People</i> might well not get hurt in the course of your bulling through the fence, but when one cultivates the traits of stone in oneself it's usually not because there was nothing in one's way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would someone who fit the Ogre description (toughening up, biding their time, becoming emotionally nigh invulnerable), but escaped in some nonviolent way be an Ogre or have no Seeming? </div> </div> </div>This is a generality beyond my ability to meaningfully speculate on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they had no Seeming, would they still look kind of like an Ogre? </div> </div> </div>I don't imagine the Ogres have a monopoly on calluses and other roughness, but in the absence of details on what parts of the Durance carry over into the mien besides the seeming I can only guess that their scars would manifest in a fashion appropriate to their kith and means of egress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T20:57:07-07:00","id":588818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=588502#post588502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Part of what's so cool about Changeling though is its like the second act of Into the Woods. It shows the aftermath of those stories. It asks what happened to Alice after she got back from Wonderland, and in doing so deconstructs the genre. Don't get me wrong, I think a story where you start out with human characters and play through their capture and their durance, culminating in the escape and gaining a Seeming would be a blast. But I think the story of what happens after that is a bit more appropriate for the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> I would also love to run or play in a Fae-Touched game, where you're going into the hedge to try to save a taken loved one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent example. The first half of that play is nice and all, but no one watches Into The Woods for it. It's the second part, where consequences follow and everyone has to grow up(Like, for reals this time), that captivates the audience.<br /> <br /> Plus they feed the narrator to the giant, which is awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T11:27:44-07:00","id":589409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584456-narrowness-of-2e-seemings?p=588635#post588635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>People</i> might well not get hurt in the course of your bulling through the fence, but when one cultivates the traits of stone in oneself it's usually not because there was nothing in one's way.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I'm the Juggernaut, bitch!&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=